Step 4: Azure File Sync

A major focus of the module was Azure File Sync.

What Azure File Sync provides:

Azure File Sync allows organizations to cache Azure file shares locally on:

On-premises Windows Servers
Cloud virtual machines
Benefits of Azure File Sync:
Faster local access to files
Centralized cloud management
Reduced on-premises storage usage
Multi-office synchronization
Cloud tiering support
Key concepts learned:
Frequently accessed files stay cached locally
Less frequently used files can remain in Azure
Users across offices access current file versions
Hybrid storage environments improve flexibility

Azure File Sync bridges traditional on-premises infrastructure with cloud storage.

Step 5: Snapshots and Soft Delete

The module covered data protection capabilities for Azure Files.

File share snapshots:

Snapshots create point-in-time backups of file shares.

Benefits:
Recover deleted files
Restore previous file versions
Protect against accidental changes
Soft delete:

Soft delete temporarily retains deleted file shares for recovery.

Key lessons:
Snapshots improve disaster recovery capabilities
Soft delete protects against accidental deletion
Data protection features are critical for organizational file systems
